Z||000008||rogergarrison||01-12-2001||09:56 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by frontal lobe:<BR><B>Vanden Plas is pronounced "vahn den plahs", and when you say it you have to kind of put your nose up a little and with your eyes kind of look down a little on the person you are saying it to in order to get the full effect.  Then ask for some GrEy (not grAy like us yanks) poupon and you are set.<P><BR>almost but not quite-correct is JAG-U-R (JAG-YOU-ARE)<BR>It's a model/trim level of a "jag-u-ah" (do NOT say "jag-wire" or you have severely blown it).</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000009||Monkeyman||01-13-2001||03:30 AM||||"Van-den Plaaas" and the Brits pronounce the vehicle (and jungle cat) "jag-you-war".  At least they did the last time I was in England (about 8 years ago).  The Jaguar Vanden Plas was the 4 door with the odd halogen headlights (as opposed to separate sealed beams) with the very upgraded trim (Connolly leather, burlwood dash & trim, etc, etc).||||reg||1
